    "headline": "Back to Night City.\nNew Crew. Same Heartbreak.",
    "subhead": "Netflix locked Cyberpunk: Edgerunners 2 for October 20, 2026 and dropped a full trailer. Ten standalone episodes, a brand-new crew, Studio Trigger at the wheel.",
    "description": "Cyberpunk: Edgerunners 2 premieres on Netflix October 20, 2026 with a new trailer and new crew. Sneakz & Beatz on the 10-episode Studio Trigger standalone.",
    "keywords": [
      "Cyberpunk Edgerunners 2",
      "Edgerunners season 2 release date",
      "Edgerunners 2 trailer",
      "Studio Trigger",
      "CD Projekt Red",
      "Netflix anime October 2026",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "Back to Night City. New Crew.",
    "ogAccent": "F5E400",
    "heroCredit": "Netflix / Studio Trigger / CD Projekt Red",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.gamesradar.com/entertainment/anime-shows/cyberpunk-edgerunners-season-2-release-date-trailer-story/",
    "trendScore": 93,
    "body": "Cyberpunk gets a beat every episode, and when it's the anime, it lives here. The update: Cyberpunk: Edgerunners 2 premieres on Netflix on October 20, 2026. The date came with a full trailer, and the trailer came with the cast.\n\n## What's confirmed\nTen episodes. A standalone story, not a direct sequel to David and Lucy. Studio Trigger animating, CD Projekt Red co-producing, and writer Bartosz Sztybor telling fans to be \"prepared for sadness.\" The four leads are D., Weak Kingsley, Roman Crarax and Talia Yang. Same Night City, different crew, different way to get chewed up by it.\n\n## Why the first one mattered\nEdgerunners in 2022 did something no game tie-in had done: it made people go back and buy the game. Cyberpunk 2077 hit its biggest player counts in years the month the anime dropped. It won the Crunchyroll Anime of the Year. It turned \"I Really Want to Stay at Your House\" into a song people cry to on the train. Trigger's animation and a story that refused a happy ending did that.\n\n## The bar for season two\nA new cast means no safety net. Nobody's tuning in for David, because David's gone. Trigger has to make you care about four strangers in ten episodes and then break your heart on schedule. The trailer says they're not softening it.\n\n## Where it sits in the Cyberpunk calendar\nTCG beta events in September, Edgerunners 2 on October 20, the trading card game's full release November 6, and Cyberpunk 2 still years out. The universe is running three formats at once and the anime is the one with the widest reach.\n\nOctober 20. Clear the night. Bring tissues.\n\n## Sources\n- GamesRadar - Edgerunners season 2 release date, trailer, story: https://www.gamesradar.com/entertainment/anime-shows/cyberpunk-edgerunners-season-2-release-date-trailer-story/\n- What's on Netflix - Edgerunners 2 sets October release, drops first trailer: https://www.whats-on-netflix.com/news/cyberpunk-edgerunners-season-2-netflix-release-date-trailer/\n- Kotaku - Edgerunners second season gets a release date: https://kotaku.com/cyberpunk-edgerunners-season-2-release-date-netflix-trailer-2000726622\n- CD Projekt Red - Edgerunners 2 official site: https://www.cyberpunk.net/en/edgerunners2",
