    "heroImage": "https://images.complex.com/complex/image/upload/c_crop,h_820,w_1182,x_0,y_0/g_auto:aoi_473_328_236_164,ar_1.91,c_fill,q_auto/sanity-new/M-06_d9ztrn",
    "trendScore": 79,
    "body": "A week out. Mowalola Ogunlesi's Air Jordan 14 collection releases Friday, September 18, per [Complex](https://www.complex.com/sneakers/a/victor-deng/mowalola-air-jordan-14-collab-2026-release-date) (@Complex) and [Nice Kicks](https://www.nicekicks.com/mowalola-air-jordan-14-sp-burnt-red-iq5708-001/): the Air Jordan 14 SP \"Burnt Red\" (IQ5708-001) at $255 and the Air Jordan 14 Mule (IR0908-001) at $180, through SNKRS, mowalola.com and select Jordan accounts.\n\n## What's in it\nThe 14 is the Ferrari shoe, Tinker's tribute to MJ's 550 Maranello, and Mowalola treats it like a car she's customizing: burnt-red suede, metallic gold detailing, her cursive signature scrawled across the lateral panel where the Jumpman crest normally sits alone. The Mule is the wild one. She sliced the 14's heel off and turned it into a slip-on, first shown at Paris Fashion Week in June. It's the most aggressive edit of a Jordan silhouette since the Off-White era, and it wasn't done by a Nike-adjacent designer; it was done by a London label that Ye once put on payroll.\n\n![Mowalola x Air Jordan 14](https://images.complex.com/complex/image/upload/c_crop,h_1350,w_1080,x_0,y_0/g_auto:aoi_432_540_216_270,q_auto,c_fill,ar_0.80,w_1200/sanity-new/M-01_qo8zyp \"Complex|https://www.complex.com/sneakers/a/victor-deng/mowalola-air-jordan-14-collab-2026-release-date\")\n\nThe apparel run matches: a co-branded jumpsuit with Mowalola's red chest stripe and a \"23\" at center, co-branding on the cuffs.\n\n## Why we're covering a collab\nSneakz keeps the sneaker lane to Air Jordan retros, and this is one: a 14, released by Jordan, on the Jordan calendar. What makes it worth the slot is who's holding the pen. Mowalola is Nigerian-born, London-raised, and one of a very short list of Black women designers who have ever been handed a Jordan silhouette outright. That is the part of the story Nike's press kit won't lead with, so we will. The [Jaide 11 Low](/the-lane/jaide-air-jordan-11-low-fiberglass-2026) drops the same day; between the two, September 18 is the most designer-driven Jordan Friday of the year.\n\n## Buy or pass\nBuy the 14 if you wear 14s and want the one pair from this year that people will ask about. The Mule is a fashion-week object; buy it because you'll wear it, not because it'll flip. At $255 the SP is priced above every GR 14 and under the CDG 11 ($255 was CDG's number too). Resale on the 14 will be real for a week and then normalize; the Mule is the one that'll hold, because nobody else is making one.\n\n## Sources\n- Complex - The Mowalola x Air Jordan 14 Collection Releases in September (updated June 24, 2026): https://www.complex.com/sneakers/a/victor-deng/mowalola-air-jordan-14-collab-2026-release-date\n- Nice Kicks - MOWALOLA x Air Jordan 14 SP \"Burnt Red\" Release Date & Info (Sept. 2026): https://www.nicekicks.com/mowalola-air-jordan-14-sp-burnt-red-iq5708-001/\n- WWD / Footwear News - Mowalola Cuts Michael Jordan's Air Jordan 14 Down to a Mule (2026): https://wwd.com/footwear-news/sneaker-news/mowalola-air-jordan-14-mule-release-date-ir0908-001-1239029522/",
    "heroFocus": "center",
