    "slug": "nintendo-direct-september-2026-switch-2-rpg-slate-persona-4-revival",
    "pillar": "gaming",
    "title": "The Switch 2 Just Became a Real RPG Machine",
    "headline": "Persona 4 Revival.\nRomancing SaGa 3.\nThe Switch 2 RPG Slate.",
    "subhead": "The September 9 Nintendo Direct was light on Mario and heavy on role-playing: Persona 4 Revival and Persona 6 confirmed for Switch 2, a Romancing SaGa 3 remake, Xenoblade 3's upgrade, FF7 Revelation preorders and Monster Hunter Wilds on December 4.",
    "description": "Nintendo Direct September 2026 RPG roundup: Persona 4 Revival on Switch 2 Feb 18, 2027, Persona 6 confirmed, Romancing SaGa 3 remake, Monster Hunter Wilds Dec 4.",
    "keywords": [
      "Nintendo Direct September 2026",
      "Persona 4 Revival Switch 2 release date",
      "Persona 6 Switch 2",
      "Romancing SaGa 3 Destinies United",
      "Monster Hunter Wilds Switch 2",
      "Final Fantasy 7 Revelation Switch 2",
      "Kingdom Come Deliverance 2 Switch 2",
      "Metroid Ravenous",
      "Kirby and the World Beyond",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "THE SWITCH 2\nRPG SLATE.",
    "ogAccent": "E60012",
    "heroCredit": "Nintendo, via GameSpot",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.gamespot.com/articles/nintendo-direct-september-2026-all-the-biggest-announcements-and-games/",
    "heroImage": "https://www.gamespot.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Nintendo-September-Direct-1.jpg",
    "trendScore": 74,
    "body": "No 3D Mario. That was the complaint after the September 9 Direct. Look past it and the show was one of the strongest single-player lineups Nintendo has put in a broadcast since the Switch 2 launched. [GameSpot's full rundown](https://www.gamespot.com/articles/nintendo-direct-september-2026-all-the-biggest-announcements-and-games/) has every trailer. Here's the RPG lane, ranked by how soon it matters.\n\n## This month and next\nFire Emblem: Fortune's Weave is out next week. Meccha Chameleon dropped the day of the show. Crisis Core: Final Fantasy VII Reunion hit Switch 2 the same day, with FF7 Revelation preorders opening for its April 2027 launch on the console. Resident Evil 2, 3 and 4 remakes land October 16. Lego Batman: Legacy of the Dark Knight is September 18.\n\n## December 4: Monster Hunter Wilds\nThe show opened with it. Wilds comes to Switch 2 on December 4 with local co-op and the Ascendance expansion included in the Switch 2 edition. For a handheld, that's the biggest third-party port of the year, and it lands two weeks after GTA 6 for anyone who needs a second screen.\n\n## The Persona news\nPersona 4: Revival is confirmed for Switch 2 on February 18, 2027, later than the PC, PS5 and Xbox versions. Then the line that got the loudest reaction: Persona 6 is coming to Switch 2 too, no date. Atlus has never committed a mainline Persona to a Nintendo platform at launch. That's a platform statement.\n\n## Remakes and ports in the lane\nRomancing SaGa 3: Destinies United is a full remake of the 1995 Square RPG with 3D graphics, rebuilt combat and voiced cutscenes, out February 16, 2027 on PC and consoles. Xenoblade Chronicles 3: Switch 2 Edition adds a Heroes Vault mode and a new hero, Shimmer. Kingdom Come: Deliverance 2 is headed to Switch 2 \"soon,\" though GameSpot called the footage rough. Eternal Anima, a new turn-based RPG, is March 4. Professor Layton and the New World of Steam is December 10. And The Witcher 3 Remastered arrives natively on September 29 with the Songs of the Past expansion to follow.\n\n## First-party, for the record\nMetroid Ravenous, the next 2D Metroid, is January 28, 2027 with an \"eat or be eaten\" hook and a talking Samus. Kirby and the World Beyond, a fully 3D open-world Kirby, closed the show for spring 2027 and the series' 35th anniversary. Mario Kart World got ten classic SNES tracks in a free update the same day. Star Fox gets four-player split-screen September 30.\n\n## The read\nNintendo is letting third parties carry the RPG weight this winter and holding its own big swings for 2027. For the single-player crowd that's fine: Wilds in December, Persona 4 and SaGa 3 in February, Metroid in January. That's a full season on one handheld.\n\n## Sources\n- GameSpot, September 9, 2026 - Nintendo Direct September 2026: All The Biggest Announcements And Games: https://www.gamespot.com/articles/nintendo-direct-september-2026-all-the-biggest-announcements-and-games/\n- Nintendo Life, September 2026 - Nintendo Direct September 2026: Every Game, Announcement And Trailer: https://www.nintendolife.com/guides/nintendo-direct-september-2026-every-game-announcement-and-trailer\n- CD PROJEKT RED Press Center, September 2026 - The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt — Remastered for Nintendo Switch 2 Featured on Latest Nintendo Direct: https://press.cdprojektred.com/en/news/1845/the-witcher-3-wild-hunt-remastered-for-nintendo-switch-2-featured-on-latest-nintendo-direct\n",
