    "trendScore": 58,
    "body": "The 6 is having a birthday year and most of the noise went to the AWAKE NY collab and the \"Salesman\" GR. In between, Jordan Brand has been using the 6 Low as the experimental lane, and the women's \"Black/Desert Berry\" is next: Wednesday, September 16, $205, per [Sneaker News](https://sneakernews.com/2026/08/24/air-jordan-6-low-black-desert-berry-ix5195-001/) (@sneakernews). Nike's product page lists it as the 6 Retro Low \"Metamorphosis.\"\n\n## The build\n\nIX5195-001. Black nubuck through the upper, metallic pink on the \"23\" heel panels, and a cooler, steelier gray on the sole for contrast. It picks up where the last two 6 Lows left off: the pony-hair \"Blackout\" and the floral \"China Rose\" take on \"Infrared.\" Same silhouette, same idea of doing something the men's 6 never would, different material story.\n\n![Air Jordan 6 Low \"Black/Desert Berry\"](https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/air-jordan-6-low-black-desert-berry-ix5195-001-5.jpg \"Sneaker News|https://sneakernews.com/2026/08/24/air-jordan-6-low-black-desert-berry-ix5195-001/\")\n\n![Air Jordan 6 Low \"Black/Desert Berry\" retailer image](https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/jordan-6-low-desert-berry-2.jpg \"Finish Line via Sneaker News|https://sneakernews.com/2026/08/24/air-jordan-6-low-black-desert-berry-ix5195-001/\")\n\n## Why the 6 Low keeps getting the weird ones\n\nThe 6 High is a canon shoe: \"Infrared,\" \"Carmine,\" the first ring. Jordan doesn't mess with it much. The Low has no OG baggage, so it's where the brand tries pony hair, florals, and now metallic pink on nubuck. For the women's line that's been the play all year, and the pairs that hit have held better than the men's GRs.\n\n## Buy notes\n\nSeptember 16, 10 a.m. ET on Nike.com, Foot Locker and Champs. Women's sizing, $205. Mid-week release, so no camping.\n\n## Sources\n- [The Air Jordan 6 Low \"Black/Desert Berry\" Drops September 16th](https://sneakernews.com/2026/08/24/air-jordan-6-low-black-desert-berry-ix5195-001/) — Sneaker News (@sneakernews), updated Sept. 2, 2026\n- [Jordan Release Dates 2026](https://sneakernews.com/air-jordan-release-dates/) — Sneaker News, Sept. 2026\n",
