    "ogHeadline": "FIVE RETROS. ONE ROOM.\nJORDAN HOLIDAY 2026 IS SET.",
    "ogAccent": "C8102E",
    "heroCredit": "Sneaker News",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/10/jordan-brand-holiday-2026-preview-nyfw/",
    "heroImage": "https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/jordan-brand-holiday-2026-preview-nyfw.jpg",
    "trendScore": 90,
    "body": "Leaks tell you what's coming. A preview suite tells you what the brand wants you to care about. During New York Fashion Week, Jordan Brand put its Holiday 2026 retros in a room and let [Sneaker News](https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/10/jordan-brand-holiday-2026-preview-nyfw/) shoot them in person. The report went up Thursday, September 10. Five shoes, five dates, no guesswork.\n\n## The calendar\n\n**Air Jordan 5 \"Halloween,\" October 17.** Black nubuck, red-orange accents, glow-in-the-dark outsole. The 5 has done Halloween before and the brand keeps coming back because the tongue and the shark teeth were built for it.\n\n**Air Jordan 12 \"Fireside,\" October 24, full family.** Light Orewood Brown, Cacao Wow, Team Red. The shoe that leaked as \"Eggnog\" and came out the other end looking like a Flu Game 12 in cocoa. [Sneaker News](https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/09/air-jordan-12-fireside-ct8013-105/) has the full breakdown.\n\n**Air Jordan 14 \"Forest Green,\" October 31, adult and grade school.** First retro since the 2005 original, and Sneaker News says the mold has been tightened up toward the OG shape.\n\n**Air Jordan 4 \"Bred,\" November 27, full family.** The OG-shaped Bred 4 is Black Friday's centerpiece. It's the shoe that makes the rest of this list a lineup instead of a schedule.\n\n**Air Jordan 10 \"Sacramento,\" December 5.** Black tumbled leather, Dark Concord in the liner and outsole. A 1995 City Pack colorway that has never been retroed until now.\n\n![Air Jordan 4 \"Bred\" at the Jordan Brand NYFW preview](https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/jordan-brand-holiday-2027-preview-at-nyfw-3.jpg \"Sneaker News|https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/10/jordan-brand-holiday-2026-preview-nyfw/\")\n\n## What the room says\n\nRead the lineup as a set and a strategy shows up. Two of the five are shoes that have never been retroed or haven't in two decades. Two are full-family drops, which means kids' sizes and the grade-school flip market on the Bred 4 and the Fireside 12. Only one, the Halloween 5, is a seasonal novelty. The rest are catalog moves, the kind of releases meant to sit in a rotation for years, not a week.\n\nThat's a shift from the 2024-25 pattern of collab-heavy holidays. The A Ma Maniére and Nina Chanel Abney energy is still around in the fall drops, but December belongs to the archive this year. Jordan is betting that a City Pack 10 and a properly shaped Bred 4 move harder than another boutique story. Given how the Fire Red 4 and Knicks 10 announcements landed last week, that bet is already paying off in attention.\n\n![Air Jordan 5 \"Halloween\" at the preview](https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/jordan-brand-holiday-2027-preview-at-nyfw-1.jpg \"Sneaker News|https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/10/jordan-brand-holiday-2026-preview-nyfw/\")\n\n## The pecking order\n\nIf the budget covers one pair, it's the Bred 4. If it covers two, add the Sacramento 10, because a first-ever retro at $205-215 is the rarest thing on this list. The Fireside 12 is the sleeper for the people who wore Cafecitos and want the same feeling without the SoleFly tax. The Forest Green 14 is the one nobody will camp for and everybody will want in February.\n\nDates are subject to Nike's usual shuffle. The room, though, was real, and the brand doesn't stage a room for shoes it plans to quietly delay.\n\n## Sources\n- [Jordan Brand Previews Holiday 2026 Retro Lineup at NYFW](https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/10/jordan-brand-holiday-2026-preview-nyfw/) — Sneaker News (@SneakerNews), Sept. 10, 2026\n- [Air Jordan 12 \"Fireside\" CT8013-105](https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/09/air-jordan-12-fireside-ct8013-105/) — Sneaker News, Sept. 9, 2026\n- [Air Jordan 10 \"Sacramento\" HJ6779-002](https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/09/air-jordan-10-sacramento-hj6779-002/) — Sneaker News, Sept. 9, 2026\n- [Air Jordan 12 Retro \"Fireside\"](https://www.soleretriever.com/sneaker-release-dates/jordan/air-jordan-12/air-jordan-12-retro-fireside-ct8013-105) — Sole Retriever (@SoleRetriever), Sept. 10, 2026\n",
