    "trendScore": 78,
    "body": "Regional exclusives are the one Jordan move that still makes Americans mad, and the \"London\" 4 is going to be the loudest one this year. [Sneaker News](https://sneakernews.com/2026/08/25/air-jordan-4-london-iv6048-001/) updated the release date to Thursday, September 17 on September 10. Nike SNKRS UK and select Jordan retailers in Europe. No US release is planned.\n\n## The shoe\n\nStyle code IV6048-001. Black/Red Bark-Dark Smoke Grey-Smoke Grey-Hemp is the official name; the shoe is a hairy grey suede 4 with black netting and a dark mudguard, closer to a rainy Tuesday than a Union Square line. $220 per Sneaker News and its release table; some aggregators have $230. Official images are out, so this is confirmed, not a leak.\n\nThe detail that makes it a London shoe and not just a grey one is the heel. The \"LDN\" lettering sits beneath a transparent heel plate, so the AIR branding and the city code both read at once. It's a small piece of engineering for a shoe that mostly sells on texture.\n\n![Air Jordan 4 \"London\" official images](https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/london-air-jordan-4-IV6048-001-1.jpg \"Nike via Sneaker News|https://sneakernews.com/2026/08/25/air-jordan-4-london-iv6048-001/\")\n\n## The city program\n\nJordan has been quietly building a city series: the Japan-only 12 \"Sumo,\" now London. The logic is the same one that made the Nike Air Max \"City\" packs work a decade ago. A shoe that only exists in one market becomes a souvenir, and souvenirs don't need hype to hold value. [Complex](https://www.complex.com/sneakers/a/victor-deng/air-jordan-4-london-release-date-iv6048-001) and [Sole Retriever](https://www.soleretriever.com/news/articles/air-jordan-4-retro-london-official-images) both have the official set.\n\nFor the US, the story is what it always is: proxies, StockX, and the 40% markup that comes with an ocean. Expect it to land at $350 to $400 in the first week and drift from there. The 4 in a muted suede has a long tail; the \"Craft\" 4s aged better than their launch numbers suggested.\n\n![Air Jordan 4 \"London\" first look](https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/jordan-4-london-1.jpg \"sneakerdenn via Sneaker News|https://sneakernews.com/2026/08/25/air-jordan-4-london-iv6048-001/\")\n\n## Verdict\n\nIf you've got a cousin in Peckham, now's the time to call. If not, wait a month. Regional 4s spike on release day and soften once the second wave of European stock hits resale. This is a good shoe, not a grail, and the price will eventually say so.\n\n## Sources\n- [Air Jordan 4 \"London\" IV6048-001 Release Date](https://sneakernews.com/2026/08/25/air-jordan-4-london-iv6048-001/) — Sneaker News (@SneakerNews), Aug. 25, 2026 (updated Sept. 10)\n- [Air Jordan 4 \"London\" Release Date](https://www.complex.com/sneakers/a/victor-deng/air-jordan-4-london-release-date-iv6048-001) — Complex (@Complex), Sept. 2026\n- [Air Jordan 4 Retro \"London\" Official Images](https://www.soleretriever.com/news/articles/air-jordan-4-retro-london-official-images) — Sole Retriever (@SoleRetriever), Sept. 2026\n- [Air Jordan 4 \"London\"](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/air-jordan-4-london-release-date/) — Sneaker Bar Detroit (@SBDsneakers), Sept. 2026\n",
    "publishedAt": "2026-09-13",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-09-13",
    "heroFocus": "center"
