    "ogHeadline": "TGS AT 30.\nFIVE DAYS. 759 EXHIBITORS.",
    "ogAccent": "107C10",
    "heroCredit": "Microsoft / Xbox Wire",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://news.xbox.com/en-us/2026/09/09/xbox-tokyo-game-show-broadcast-announce-2026/",
    "heroImage": "https://xboxwire.thesourcemediaassets.com/sites/2/2026/09/TGS_AnnounceStatic_2026-814e275774b1b96bd7e9.jpg",
    "trendScore": 70,
    "body": "Tokyo Game Show is the one industry event that never got smaller. This year it's the biggest it's ever been: five days for the first time, September 17 through 21 at Makuhari Messe, with 759 exhibitors for the 30th anniversary. Business days are Wednesday and Thursday; the public gets Friday through Sunday. [VGC](https://www.videogameschronicle.com/news/tokyo-game-show-2026-unveils-exhibitor-list-including-playstation-and-square-enix/) and [Gematsu](https://www.gematsu.com/2026/07/tokyo-game-show-2026-exhibitors-list-and-main-visual-announced) have the exhibitor list.\n\n## Xbox goes first\n\nThe only confirmed first-party broadcast is Microsoft's. [Xbox Wire](https://news.xbox.com/en-us/2026/09/09/xbox-tokyo-game-show-broadcast-announce-2026/) announced on September 9 that the Xbox TGS Broadcast airs Thursday, September 17 at 7 p.m. JST, which is 3 a.m. Pacific and 6 a.m. Eastern. About 50 minutes, hosted by Misuzu Araki, on the TGS, Xbox and Xbox Japan YouTube channels plus Twitch.\n\nThe two named headliners are Minecraft Dungeons II, making its show-floor debut ahead of a day-one Game Pass launch on September 29, and Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 4 multiplayer, playable at the show through Xbox's partnership with Happinet before the October 23 launch. There's a FanFest Tokyo watch party the same night with Araki and Larry Hryb. [Pure Xbox](https://www.purexbox.com/news/2026/09/xbox-reveals-more-of-what-to-expect-from-tokyo-game-show-showcase-next-week) has the rundown. Anything about Death Stranding 2 or other PlayStation ports showing up on Xbox is fan speculation until the stream says otherwise.\n\n![Xbox at Tokyo Game Show 2026](https://xboxwire.thesourcemediaassets.com/sites/2/2026/09/TGS_AnnounceStatic_2026-814e275774b1b96bd7e9.jpg \"Microsoft / Xbox Wire|https://news.xbox.com/en-us/2026/09/09/xbox-tokyo-game-show-broadcast-announce-2026/\")\n\n## The floor\n\nSony Interactive is exhibiting. So are Sega/Atlus with Stranger Than Heaven, Persona 4 Revival, Crazy Taxi World Tour, Metaphor: ReFantazio on Switch 2 and Sonic Racing CrossWorlds; Konami with Silent Hill: Townfall, Castlevania: Belmont's Curse and Suikoden STAR LEAP; and Square Enix, Capcom, Bandai Namco, Koei Tecmo, Game Freak, LEVEL-5, Nexon and Pocketpair. Konami's [official lineup](https://www.konami.com/games/tgs/en/lineup/) is already posted. Nintendo isn't there, because Nintendo is never there.\n\nFor the people who care about hardware, there's a 30th Anniversary Ticket that comes with a gold medal engraved with game art, which is the most Japanese collectible of the year.\n\n## Why it matters over here\n\nTGS is where the Japanese publishers show what they're actually shipping in 2027, and the last two years of Western showcases have been mostly GTA 6 counter-programming. Silent Hill: Townfall and Persona 4 Revival are the two games most likely to get real dates this week. Xbox is spending money in Japan for the first time in a while, which tells you where it thinks the next console war is being fought. And Modern Warfare 4 going hands-on in Tokyo five weeks before launch is the kind of confidence Activision only shows when the beta went well.\n\nSet an alarm for 3 a.m. Thursday, or don't. The clips will be everywhere by breakfast.\n\n## Sources\n- [XBOX @ Tokyo Game Show 2026](https://news.xbox.com/en-us/2026/09/09/xbox-tokyo-game-show-broadcast-announce-2026/) — Xbox Wire (@Xbox), Sept. 9, 2026\n- [Tokyo Game Show 2026 unveils exhibitor list including PlayStation and Square Enix](https://www.videogameschronicle.com/news/tokyo-game-show-2026-unveils-exhibitor-list-including-playstation-and-square-enix/) — VGC, 2026\n- [Tokyo Game Show 2026 exhibitors list and main visual announced](https://www.gematsu.com/2026/07/tokyo-game-show-2026-exhibitors-list-and-main-visual-announced) — Gematsu, July 2026\n- [Xbox reveals more of what to expect from Tokyo Game Show showcase](https://www.purexbox.com/news/2026/09/xbox-reveals-more-of-what-to-expect-from-tokyo-game-show-showcase-next-week) — Pure Xbox, Sept. 2026\n- [Konami TGS 2026 lineup](https://www.konami.com/games/tgs/en/lineup/) — Konami, Sept. 2026\n",
