    "trendScore": 52,
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "body": "Solo Leveling proved a Korean webtoon can be the biggest anime of a season. Overgeared is the next one in line, and it's three weeks out.\n\n## The update\nPer [Anime News Network](https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-09-13/overgeared-anime-reveals-3rd-trailer-2-new-cast-members/.241725) on September 13: third trailer, third key visual, two new cast members. Premiere is October 2 on Tokyo MX at 11:30pm Japan time, which is 10:30am Eastern the same day, with Crunchyroll streaming. J.C.Staff animates, Ayako Kono directs, and the opening is \"SATISFY\" by Re:name. It was also one of the five previews on Crunchyroll's Anime Nights bill with Black Clover Season 2 on September 21.\n\n## What it is\nGrid is the worst player in the VR game Satisfy until he stumbles into a legendary class: Pagma's Successor, the blacksmith. Instead of leveling faster than everyone, he crafts gear nobody else can make. Same power-fantasy engine as Solo Leveling, different trade. The webtoon has been a top-five title on Webtoon and Tapas for years.\n\n## Why it's here\nBig-name rule: this is the biggest manhwa adaptation of the fall, and the Solo Leveling audience is the show's audience. October 2 is close enough to matter, and it's the last of the Anime Nights five to lock its details.\n\n## Sources\n- Anime News Network, Sept. 13, 2026 — Overgeared anime reveals 3rd trailer, 2 new cast members: https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-09-13/overgeared-anime-reveals-3rd-trailer-2-new-cast-members/.241725\n"
