    "ogHeadline": "MC LYTE'S ROAD\nTO THE HALL OF FAME.",
    "ogAccent": "B8862B",
    "heroCredit": "Patrick Neree via AllHipHop",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://allhiphop.com/exclusives/mc-lyte-takes-road-to-the-hall-of-fame-with-12-city-tour/",
    "trendScore": 70,
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "body": "The first solo woman in rap to release a full album is walking into the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame on November 14. She's not flying straight there. MC Lyte told AllHipHop's Chuck Creekmur she's doing 12 cities first, and most of them are places that built her.\n\n## The dates\nSeptember 24, Washington, D.C., at the Smithsonian's National Museum of African American History and Culture for its 10th anniversary. September 25, Tulsa, Black Wall Street Nation. October 1, Cleveland. October 9, Norfolk State homecoming. October 11, Brooklyn Bowl. October 12, Pittsburgh. October 13, Philadelphia. October 14, Hudson Valley. October 15, Boston. October 17, St. Louis, two shows. October 20, Chicago, two shows. October 21, Minneapolis. November 9 and 10, Atlanta. November 11, Nashville. Three days later, Los Angeles, and the Musical Influence Award.\n\n## The show\nNinety minutes, she says, and \"we're going to go through the catalog.\" She named \"I Am the Lyte,\" the Grand Puba record, as one she's pulling back out. Stories between the songs, conversation with the room, no parade of surprise guests holding the set together. \"Thank God, because of the catalog that I have, I don't really need to pull out a bunch of stops.\"\n\n## Why it lands\nLyte's Lyte As a Rock came out in 1988. She's been the standard for clarity on a mic for almost four decades, and the cities on this list are the ones that showed up before the industry did. \"It feels like I'm just returning home.\" A Hall of Fame plaque is one kind of recognition. Selling out City Winery in Pittsburgh on a Monday is the other kind.\n\n## Sources\n- AllHipHop, Sept. 10, 2026, MC Lyte takes \"Road to the Hall of Fame\" with 12-city tour (exclusive): https://allhiphop.com/exclusives/mc-lyte-takes-road-to-the-hall-of-fame-with-12-city-tour/\n- Rock & Roll Hall of Fame, MC Lyte inductee page: https://rockhall.com/inductees/mc-lyte/\n- MC Lyte tour tickets hub: https://www.flow.page/1of1tour\n"
