    "trendScore": 76,
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "body": "Say \"reportedly\" before every sentence of this one. Sneaker News published a report on September 14 that Travis Scott's next Air Jordan 1 Low is an OG red \"Chicago\" colorway, targeted for 2027. That's the whole fact set.\n\n## What's reported\nA reverse-Swoosh 1 Low in the red, white, and black of the 1985 Chicago 1. No style code, no price, no season beyond \"2027,\" no official images. Neither Cactus Jack nor Jordan Brand has said anything. Sneaker News' track record on Travis pairs is good, which is why it's worth a line; it is still a report.\n\n## Why it moves anyway\nTravis's 1 Lows are the most flipped Jordans of the decade: the Mocha, the Fragment, the Olive, the Canary, the Velvet Brown. A red one ties the reverse Swoosh to the most famous Jordan colorway there is. That's not a shoe, that's a resell event, and it will get treated like one the second an image leaks.\n\n## The other 2027 whisper\nSole Retriever reported on September 11 that a \"Blue Ferrari\" Air Jordan 14 is set for fall 2027, a blue counterpart to the red Ferrari 14 from 2014 and the Maranello that just anchored Mike's car auction. Also unconfirmed. Also fine to know about.\n\n## Sources\n- Sneaker News, Sept. 14, 2026, Travis Scott Air Jordan 1 Low OG \"red Chicago\" report: https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/14/travis-scott-air-jordan-1-low-og-red-chicago/\n- Sole Retriever, Sept. 11, 2026, the Air Jordan 14 is set to get a Blue Ferrari colorway: https://www.soleretriever.com/news/articles/air-jordan-14-retro-blue-ferrari-release-date-fall-2027\n"
