    "ogHeadline": "MIKE McFARLAND,\n1970–2026.",
    "ogAccent": "555555",
    "heroCredit": "Deadline",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://deadline.com/2026/09/mike-mcfarland-dead-one-piece-dragon-ball-z-1237073700/",
    "trendScore": 74,
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "body": "Mike McFarland died on September 10. He was 56. Glioblastoma, diagnosed in 2025. If you watched Dragon Ball Z on Toonami, you heard him every week and probably never knew his name.\n\n## The roles\nMaster Roshi in Dragon Ball, Dragon Ball Z, and everything after. Buggy the Clown in One Piece. Jean Kirstein in Attack on Titan. Jean Havoc in Fullmetal Alchemist and Brotherhood. Teppei Sugo in Psycho-Pass. Each one a different register, and Roshi in particular is the kind of performance that gets imitated at every convention for thirty years.\n\n## The other job\nMcFarland was one of the original Funimation people in Texas: ADR director, script writer, line producer, the person in the booth telling the person on the mic how to land a line. He directed hundreds of episodes, including large stretches of Dragon Ball Z, which means the English-language version of that show sounds the way it does in part because of decisions he made. When Funimation folded into Crunchyroll he kept working. Deadline called him one of the most influential figures in Texas-based anime production, which is a quiet way of saying he helped build the American dub industry.\n\n## What to do\nWatch an episode with Roshi in it. Say the name. That's the whole tribute.\n\n## Sources\n- Deadline, Sept. 2026, Mike McFarland dies: One Piece, Dragon Ball Z voice actor was 56: https://deadline.com/2026/09/mike-mcfarland-dead-one-piece-dragon-ball-z-1237073700/\n- Variety, Sept. 2026, Mike McFarland, One Piece and Dragon Ball Z voice actor, dies at 56: https://variety.com/2026/film/people-news/mike-mcfarland-dead-dragon-ball-z-one-piece-1236857755/\n- Anime News Network, Sept. 10, 2026, voice actor Mike McFarland dies at 56: https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-09-10/voice-actor-mike-mcfarland-dies-at-56/.241616\n"
