    "ogHeadline": "HOV TOOK THE MET.\nHBO GETS IT FRIDAY.",
    "ogAccent": "C9A227",
    "heroCredit": "Roc Nation via Hot 97",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.hot97.com/news/jay-z-and-rick-rubin-premiere-jay-z-in-8-at-the-metropolitan-opera-house/",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "trendScore": 91,
    "body": "Hov took the Met. Not Yankee Stadium, not Stade de France. The Metropolitan Opera House at Lincoln Center, tuxedo on, Rick Rubin next to him, and a room full of people who came to watch him talk about his own bars.\n\n## What happened\nSunday night, September 13, [@Hot97](https://www.hot97.com/news/jay-z-and-rick-rubin-premiere-jay-z-in-8-at-the-metropolitan-opera-house/) was on the carpet as JAŸ-Z and Rubin premiered *JAŸ-Z In 8*, the eight-part HBO Original that hits HBO and HBO Max this Friday, September 18. [Complex](https://www.complex.com/style/a/tracewilliamcowen/jay-z-rick-rubin-docuseries-premiere) and [Essence](https://www.essence.com/entertainment/inside-jay-z-in-8-premiere-in-nyc/) filled in the room: Beyoncé, Leonardo DiCaprio, SZA, Daniel Kaluuya, DJ Khaled, Fat Joe, Gunna, Yo Gotti, Questlove, Jerrod Carmichael, Winnie Harlow, Lindsey Vonn, Robert Kraft, Michael Rubin. Screening inside, D'USSÉ after-party on Lincoln Center Plaza. Roc Nation shot the whole thing like a state function, because that's what it was.\n\n![Jay-Z in a tuxedo on the JAŸ-Z In 8 red carpet at the Metropolitan Opera House](https://images.complex.com/complex/image/upload/c_crop,h_1081,w_1920,x_0,y_0/g_auto:aoi_768_433_384_216,ar_1.91,c_fill,q_auto,w_1200/sanity-new/pesfrhlc6anwsyekbg25 \"Roc Nation via Complex|https://www.complex.com/style/a/tracewilliamcowen/jay-z-rick-rubin-docuseries-premiere\")\n\nThe tux got its own news cycle. Complex clocked fans tying the look back to earlier Hov eras, which is the whole point of a project built on looking back.\n\n## What the series actually is\nRubin interviews, directs and executive produces, his documentary directorial debut, and the format is the *McCartney 3, 2, 1* setup pointed at Brooklyn: two men, a table, a catalog. Eight episodes, eight projects. *Reasonable Doubt*, *Vol. 3*, *The Dynasty*, *The Blueprint*, *The Black Album*, *American Gangster*, *Watch the Throne*, *4:44*. Per [Billboard](https://www.billboard.com/culture/tv-film/jay-z-rick-rubin-hbo-max-docuseries-release-date-trailer-1236324532/) and [Hot 97](https://www.hot97.com/news/jay-z-and-rick-rubin-premiere-jay-z-in-8-at-the-metropolitan-opera-house/), the records on the table include \"Can't Knock the Hustle,\" \"Can I Live,\" \"Where I'm From,\" \"Brooklyn's Finest,\" \"99 Problems,\" \"What More Can I Say,\" \"Meet the Parents,\" \"No Church in the Wild,\" \"The Story of O.J.,\" \"Family Feud,\" \"4:44\" and \"Legacy.\" Kaluuya exec produces alongside Jay and Rubin.\n\n!youtube(https://youtu.be/xEMniH7jzs4)\n\nRollout: two episodes Friday, September 18 at 8 p.m. ET/PT on HBO, streaming on HBO Max the same minute, then two new ones every Friday through October 9.\n\n## Why this one matters\nJay does not do access. Thirty years in and the closest we've had to him explaining the writing is a handful of interviews and *Decoded*. This is eight hours of him line-reading his own catalog to the man who built Def Jam's sound before Jay ever walked into it. The Stade de France run, the Tottenham dates, [the Yankee Stadium freestyle Kaepernick is still arguing about](/the-lane/colin-kaepernick-jay-z-yankee-stadium-freestyle-guilty-conscience-2026), the *Blueprint* at 25 sitting at No. 1 on Apple Music's rap chart this week. All of it is the same campaign: own the legacy before anybody else narrates it. [We said it after Paris](/the-lane/jay-z-stade-de-france-pharrell-timberlake-jay-z-30-tour-2026). The doc is the receipt.\n\nThen SoFi, October 23 and 24, and whatever the Roc Nation \"stay tuned\" was actually about.\n\n## Sources\n- [JAŸ-Z and Rick Rubin Premiere 'JAŸ-Z In 8' at the Metropolitan Opera House](https://www.hot97.com/news/jay-z-and-rick-rubin-premiere-jay-z-in-8-at-the-metropolitan-opera-house/) — Hot 97, Sept. 14, 2026\n- [Jay-Z Opts for Timeless Tux Look at World Premiere of Rick Rubin-Directed Docuseries](https://www.complex.com/style/a/tracewilliamcowen/jay-z-rick-rubin-docuseries-premiere) — Complex, Sept. 14, 2026\n- [Inside JAŸ-Z's Star-Studded 'JAŸ-Z In 8' Premiere In New York City](https://www.essence.com/entertainment/inside-jay-z-in-8-premiere-in-nyc/) — Essence, Sept. 14, 2026\n- [JAŸ-Z Brings Out All The Stars At Premiere For \"JAŸ-Z In 8\"](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1009673-jay-z-in-8-premiere) — HotNewHipHop, Sept. 14, 2026\n- [JAŸ-Z & Rick Rubin's HBO Max Docuseries Lands A Release Date](https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/1007288-jay-z-rick-rubin-docuseries-release-date) — HotNewHipHop, Aug. 26, 2026\n- [Jay-Z, Rick Rubin HBO Max docuseries release date + trailer](https://www.billboard.com/culture/tv-film/jay-z-rick-rubin-hbo-max-docuseries-release-date-trailer-1236324532/) — Billboard, Aug. 26, 2026\n- [JAŸ-Z In 8 official trailer](https://youtu.be/xEMniH7jzs4) — HBO Max, YouTube\n",
    "heroImage": "https://www.hot97.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/HBO_CAPTURE_JAY_SELECTS-13-e1789406124551.jpg?resize=2000,1333"
