    "body": "The most-anticipated villain in *JoJo's* finally has a face in motion. Netflix dropped the *Steel Ball Run* 2nd STAGE trailer on Monday, Sept. 14, and Funny Valentine is in it.\n\n## What's in the trailer\nThree reveals, per [Netflix Tudum](https://www.netflix.com/tudum/articles/steel-ball-run-jojos-bizarre-adventure-release-date-news): Mountain Tim, Hot Pants and President Funny Valentine himself. Anyone who's read Part 7 knows why the last one matters; anyone who hasn't should stay off the wiki for the next two years.\n\n!youtube(https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gCzOb1mV2TY)\n\n## The schedule\nAs we [reported last week](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/jojo-steel-ball-run-2nd-stage-netflix-weekly-september-25-2026), 2nd STAGE streams from Friday, Sept. 25, one episode a week on Fridays. What's new is the count: eleven episodes in this cour, per Tudum and [GamesRadar](https://www.gamesradar.com/entertainment/anime-shows/jojos-bizarre-adventure-steel-ball-run-release-date-time-schedule-netflix/), covering roughly 750 miles of desert through the Devil's Palm. 1st STAGE was a single 47-minute premiere back on March 19. Yasuhiro Kimura and Hideya Takahashi direct, the same crew as prior JoJo seasons. GamesRadar also carries a leak we'll label a leak: 11 episodes in 2026, 22 in 2027, 9 in 2028, for somewhere around 42 total. Netflix hasn't confirmed anything past this cour.\n\n## The dub\nEnglish cast per Tudum: Daman Mills as Johnny Joestar, Kaiji Tang as Gyro Zeppeli, Damien Haas as Diego Brando, Frankie Kevich as Lucy Steel, Jamieson Price as Steven Steel, Alejandro Antonio Ruiz as Sandman, Cedric Williams as Pocoloco.\n\n## Why weekly matters\nNetflix's binge-drop model killed *Stone Ocean*'s conversation in 2022; the whole season came and went in three batches and the internet never got to argue about it. Weekly Fridays for *Steel Ball Run*, the part most fans call the best in the series, is Netflix admitting that the way anime spreads is through a Friday-night argument, not a weekend of autoplay.\n\n## Sources\n- Netflix Tudum, Sept. 14, 2026, Steel Ball Run 2nd STAGE trailer and release news: https://www.netflix.com/tudum/articles/steel-ball-run-jojos-bizarre-adventure-release-date-news\n- GamesRadar, Sept. 2026, Steel Ball Run release date, time and schedule: https://www.gamesradar.com/entertainment/anime-shows/jojos-bizarre-adventure-steel-ball-run-release-date-time-schedule-netflix/\n",
