    "ogHeadline": "42 POINTS IN OLD 1s.\nNOW IT'S A SHOE.",
    "ogAccent": "C8102E",
    "heroImage": "https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/air-jordan-1-low-og-last-dance-in-the-garden-ir0088-001-5.jpg",
    "heroCredit": "Sneaker News / Nike",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/14/air-jordan-1-low-og-last-dance-in-the-garden-ir0088-001/",
    "trendScore": 83,
    "body": "We [wrote it up](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/air-jordan-1-low-og-last-dance-at-the-garden-ir0088-001-fat-joe-september-26-2026) when Fat Joe had it on. Now the official images are out, and the details are better than the teases.\n\n## The game, one more time\nMarch 8, 1998. MJ's last game as a Bull at Madison Square Garden. He benched the 13s, laced up a pair of old \"Chicago\" 1s, played through bloody blisters and put up 42 in a Chicago win. It's the origin story of the Jordan 1 as a flex, not a basketball shoe.\n\n## What the official images confirm\nPer [Sneaker News](https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/14/air-jordan-1-low-og-last-dance-in-the-garden-ir0088-001/) (Sept. 14), the Air Jordan 1 Low OG \"Last Dance at the Garden,\" IR0088-001, blocks like a Chicago with red floral stitching on the toe, eyelets and heel. Metallic gold on the Wings logo and the lower eyelets. A black Swoosh laid over metallic gold leather. The inner tongue carries the game date and MJ's box score; the outer tongue accent is Knicks blue and orange. Pink insoles with blue-and-orange Nike Air. [House of Heat](https://houseofheat.co/jordan/air-jordan-1-low-og-last-dance-at-the-garden-ir0088-001) confirms packaging includes a card with an MJ quote about coming back to play the Garden.\n\n![Air Jordan 1 Low OG Last Dance at the Garden, official image](https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/air-jordan-1-low-og-last-dance-in-the-garden-ir0088-001-1.jpg \"Sneaker News / Nike|https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/14/air-jordan-1-low-og-last-dance-in-the-garden-ir0088-001/\")\n\n## Release\nSaturday, Sept. 26, 2026, $155, 10 a.m. ET, per the [Sneaker News Jordan calendar](https://sneakernews.com/air-jordan-release-dates/): Nike SNKRS, Nikestore, Foot Locker, SNIPES, Sneaker Politics and TAKOUT NY. [Sole Retriever](https://www.soleretriever.com/news/articles/air-jordan-1-retro-low-last-dance-at-the-garden-official-images) has the same set of official images.\n\n![Air Jordan 1 Low OG Last Dance at the Garden, tongue detail](https://sneakernews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/air-jordan-1-low-og-last-dance-in-the-garden-ir0088-001-9.jpg \"Sneaker News / Nike|https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/14/air-jordan-1-low-og-last-dance-in-the-garden-ir0088-001/\")\n\n## The read\nThis is the second New York Jordan story of the week, next to the [Knicks 8](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/air-jordan-8-knicks-ix8479-010-first-official-images-december-24-2026), and it's the more interesting one for storytelling: a Chicago shoe in Knicks accents, honoring the night MJ embarrassed the Garden in his own retro. Jordan Brand has been leaning on these narrative Lows since the \"Chicago\" reissues, and the box-score tongue is the kind of detail that ages well. At $155 with a wide retailer list, it should be gettable. That's rare for a 1 with a story this good.\n\n## Sources\n- Sneaker News, Sept. 14, 2026, Air Jordan 1 Low OG \"Last Dance in the Garden\" IR0088-001: https://sneakernews.com/2026/09/14/air-jordan-1-low-og-last-dance-in-the-garden-ir0088-001/\n- House of Heat, Air Jordan 1 Low OG \"Last Dance at the Garden\": https://houseofheat.co/jordan/air-jordan-1-low-og-last-dance-at-the-garden-ir0088-001\n- Sole Retriever, official images: https://www.soleretriever.com/news/articles/air-jordan-1-retro-low-last-dance-at-the-garden-official-images\n- Sneaker Bar Detroit: https://sneakerbardetroit.com/air-jordan-1-low-og-last-dance-in-the-garden/\n",
