    "trendScore": 70,
    "body": "This is how a collab gets confirmed in 2026: not a press release, not a teaser, a boutique co-founder replying to a comment. Label it accordingly. There is no product photo yet, and the image above is SBD's graphic, not the shoe.\n\n## What was said\nPer [Sneaker Bar Detroit](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/solefly-air-jordan-4/) on Sept. 17, SoleFly co-founder Daniel Hidalgo confirmed a SoleFly x Air Jordan 4 is coming, in an Instagram comment under a post about the University of Miami's expected move from adidas back to Nike. The only detail: \"soon.\" No colorway, no materials, no release date.\n\n![SoleFly Instagram comment confirming the Air Jordan 4](https://sneakerbardetroit.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/solefly-air-jordan-4-info.webp \"Sneaker Bar Detroit|https://sneakerbardetroit.com/solefly-air-jordan-4/\")\n\n## What's reported, not confirmed\nMiami is expected to leave adidas for Nike in July 2027 on a reported 10-year deal. That's reporting, not an announcement. SBD is careful to note that Hidalgo did not confirm the AJ4 as a Hurricanes project; the comment thread just happened to be about the school. Given SoleFly's history, the Miami read is reasonable, but it is a read.\n\n## The SoleFly track record\nThe AJ12 \"Cafecito\" took Miami coffee culture and turned it into one of the best Jordan collabs of the 2020s. Earlier SoleFly 1s and 3s used Hurricanes-adjacent orange and green. The boutique's next confirmed drop is closer: the SoleFly x Air Jordan 5 (IU0734-001), Black/Aurora Green/Anthracite/Muslin, listed for Oct. 8 at SoleFly per the [Sneaker News calendar](https://sneakernews.com/air-jordan-release-dates/).\n\n## The read\nA Miami boutique on a 4 is the right silhouette at the right time; the [J Balvin \"Lemonade\"](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/j-balvin-air-jordan-4-lemonade-september-25-2026) drops this Friday and the [Bred OG](https://sneakzandbeatz.com/the-lane/air-jordan-4-bred-og-black-friday-nyfw-first-look-2026) owns Black Friday, so the 4 is having a year. Until SoleFly posts a shoe, everything else is a comment section. We'll update when there's leather to look at.\n\n## Sources\n- Sneaker Bar Detroit, Sept. 17, 2026, SoleFly x Air Jordan 4 confirmed: https://sneakerbardetroit.com/solefly-air-jordan-4/\n- Sneaker News Jordan release calendar, SoleFly x Air Jordan 5 Oct. 8 entry: https://sneakernews.com/air-jordan-release-dates/\n",
