    "title": "Persona 4 Revival Makes Aika a Social Link",
    "headline": "Persona 4 Revival Turns\nAika Into a Social Link",
    "subhead": "Atlus used the second Persona 4 Revival broadcast on September 20 to confirm Aika Nakamura, the Aiya delivery girl from Persona 4: The Animation, as a brand-new Social Link, tied to a new 'Location Episodes' system. February 2027.",
    "description": "Persona 4 Revival adds Aika Nakamura from the 2011 anime as a new Social Link with Location Episodes, Atlus confirmed Sept. 20. It launches February 2027.",
    "keywords": [
      "Persona 4 Revival",
      "Aika Nakamura",
      "Persona 4 Revival social link",
      "Persona 4 Revival broadcast episode 2",
      "Location Episodes Persona 4",
      "Persona 4 The Animation",
      "Persona 4 Revival release date February 2027",
      "Atlus",
      "Persona 4 Golden remake",
      "Aiya Inaba",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "Black-owned media"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "PERSONA 4 REVIVAL TURNS\nAIKA INTO A SOCIAL LINK",
    "ogAccent": "6B1E2A",
    "heroCredit": "Atlus",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.gamesradar.com/games/persona/persona-4-revival-adds-a-fan-favorite-character-from-the-anime-as-a-social-link-hinting-we-might-get-new-personas-in-the-remake/",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "trendScore": 78,
    "body": "If you played Persona 4 Golden, you ate at Aiya. If you took the Mighty Beef Bowl challenge enough times, you heard about the owners' daughter who was always out on delivery. You never met her. Revival fixes that.\n\n## What Atlus said\nEpisode 2 of the Persona 4 Revival Broadcast streamed on September 20 and confirmed Aika Nakamura as a new Social Link ([Game8](https://game8.co/articles/latest/persona-4-revival-confirms-aika-nakamura-as-new-social-link-character), [Final Weapon](https://finalweapon.net/2026/09/19/persona-4-revival-aika-nakamura-social-link/)). She's a classmate, she still runs deliveries for Aiya in the Central Shopping District, and Atlus introduced her as \"laid back by nature.\" She originated in Persona 4: The Animation in 2011 and was never in the game. Now she's canon ([GamesRadar](https://www.gamesradar.com/games/persona/persona-4-revival-adds-a-fan-favorite-character-from-the-anime-as-a-social-link-hinting-we-might-get-new-personas-in-the-remake/)).\n\n## Location Episodes\nAika is part of a new mechanic called Location Episodes, where you learn stories about how the cast behaved in the past, tied to places around Inaba ([RPGamer](https://rpgamer.com/2026/09/persona-4-revival-broadcasts-additional-game-details/), [GoNintendo](https://gonintendo.com/contents/65229-persona-4-revival-location-episodes-new-social-link-soundtrack-details-and-more)). It's the kind of side-content Persona 3 Reload added around the edges, and it's the first sign that Revival is doing more than repainting Golden.\n\n## The question a new link raises\nA Social Link means an Arcana. A new Arcana usually means new Personas to fuse. GamesRadar flagged the obvious follow-up: does Aika come with a card of her own, and if so, what's in the Compendium that wasn't there before? Atlus didn't say. The broadcast also didn't detail her storyline.\n\n## The bigger remake picture\nRevival is already changing things fans argued about for a decade. Marie, the Golden addition that never sat right, is being woven in more naturally. A couple of Yosuke scenes were adjusted. The entire English voice cast was replaced, which split the room. MAPPA handles the cutscenes. It launches in February 2027.\n\n## The take\nPersona games live on the calendar and the people you choose to spend it with. Adding one more person to that calendar, one the anime crowd has loved for fifteen years, is a smart way to make a faithful remake feel new without touching the murder mystery. The delivery girl finally gets a scene. Inaba's getting bigger.\n\n## Sources\n- [Persona 4 Revival adds a fan-favorite character from the anime as a social link](https://www.gamesradar.com/games/persona/persona-4-revival-adds-a-fan-favorite-character-from-the-anime-as-a-social-link-hinting-we-might-get-new-personas-in-the-remake/) — GamesRadar+, Sept. 20, 2026\n- [Persona 4 Revival confirms Aika Nakamura as a new Social Link character](https://game8.co/articles/latest/persona-4-revival-confirms-aika-nakamura-as-new-social-link-character) — Game8, Sept. 2026\n- [Persona 4 Revival Broadcast reveals Aika Nakamura as new Social Link](https://finalweapon.net/2026/09/19/persona-4-revival-aika-nakamura-social-link/) — Final Weapon, Sept. 19, 2026\n- [Persona 4 Revival broadcasts additional game details](https://rpgamer.com/2026/09/persona-4-revival-broadcasts-additional-game-details/) — RPGamer, Sept. 2026\n- [Persona 4 Revival Location Episodes, new Social Link, soundtrack details](https://gonintendo.com/contents/65229-persona-4-revival-location-episodes-new-social-link-soundtrack-details-and-more) — GoNintendo, Sept. 2026\n",
    "publishedAt": "2026-09-21",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-09-21"
