    "slug": "crunchyroll-fall-2026-anime-season-opens-september-26-apothecary-diaries-black-clover-firefly-wedding",
    "pillar": "anime",
    "title": "Fall Anime Starts Saturday. Here's the Week-One Map.",
    "headline": "Fall Anime Starts Saturday.\nHere's the Map.",
    "subhead": "Crunchyroll's Fall 2026 slate opens Sept. 26 with 40-plus simulcasts: 'Overgeared' Sept. 27, 'The Apothecary Diaries' Season 3 Oct. 2, 'Black Clover' Season 2 Oct. 3, 'Firefly Wedding' Oct. 9. The culture picks, dated.",
    "description": "Crunchyroll's Fall 2026 anime season opens Sept. 26. A dated guide to the series that matter: Overgeared, Apothecary Diaries S3, Black Clover S2, Aoashi S2, Firefly Wedding.",
    "keywords": [
      "Fall 2026 anime",
      "Crunchyroll Fall 2026",
      "Black Clover Season 2",
      "The Apothecary Diaries Season 3",
      "Overgeared anime",
      "Firefly Wedding anime",
      "Aoashi Season 2",
      "Magic Knight Rayearth 2026",
      "The Vermilion Mask",
      "PSYREN anime",
      "fall anime premiere dates",
      "anime September 26 2026",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "Black-owned media"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "FALL ANIME STARTS SATURDAY.\nHERE'S THE MAP.",
    "ogAccent": "F47521",
    "heroImage": "https://www.awn.com/sites/default/files/styles/large_featured/public/image/featured/download-1280.jpg?itok=Dig1dLQM",
    "heroCredit": "Crunchyroll via Animation World Network",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.awn.com/news/crunchyroll-announces-massive-fall-2026-anime-lineup",
    "trendScore": 60,
    "body": "The season starts Saturday, September 26, and the lineup Crunchyroll [published September 15](https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/seasonal-lineup/2026/9/15/fall-anime-2026-crunchyroll) runs more than 40 series. Most of it is isekai wallpaper. Here's the part worth your Saturday.\n\n!youtube(https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zjTA2uE_y_8)\n\n## The first weekend\n**Sept. 26:** *A Wild Last Boss Appeared!* Season 2 gets an early premiere. **Sept. 27:** *Overgeared* (J.C.STAFF), the Korean webnovel adaptation about a broke gamer who becomes a god-tier blacksmith in a VR game. Manhwa-to-anime has been the growth lane for three years (*Solo Leveling* being the proof), and this is the season's big swing at it. Full English dub at launch, per [AWN](https://www.awn.com/news/crunchyroll-announces-massive-fall-2026-anime-lineup). If you've been at Dream Con, you know this audience.\n\n## The big returns\n**Oct. 2:** *The Apothecary Diaries* Season 3 (OLM). The show that got a whole generation of non-anime people to watch a mystery series about a court pharmacist. **Oct. 3:** *Black Clover* Season 2 (Pierrot), five years after the first run ended, picking up the Spade Kingdom raid. Crunchyroll put it in theaters tonight ([Anime Nights, Sept. 21](/the-lane/black-clover-season-2-theaters-september-21-crunchyroll-anime-nights-2026)) because Asta is the shonen protagonist this audience adopted hardest after Naruto. **Oct. 4:** *Aoashi* Season 2 (TMS), the football anime that got real footballers watching anime; U-18 Premier League arc, Ashito on the A team. **Oct. 7:** *Magic Knight Rayearth*, the CLAMP remake we [broke down yesterday](/the-lane/magic-knight-rayearth-2026-remake-trailer-theme-songs-cast-october-7-clamp).\n\n![A Wild Last Boss Appeared! Season 2](https://www.awn.com/sites/default/files/styles/inline/public/image/attached/1081399-awildlastbossappeared16x93840x2160-1280.jpg?itok=lX5mCuSn \"Touya / EARTH STAR Entertainment via AWN|https://www.awn.com/news/crunchyroll-announces-massive-fall-2026-anime-lineup\")\n\n## The new ones\n**Oct. 9:** *Firefly Wedding* (david production), the Taisho-era noblewoman-hires-an-assassin romance, with a 12-language dub out of the gate, which is Crunchyroll telling you where the marketing money went. **Oct. 10:** *The Vermilion Mask* (100studio), a globe-trotting revenge story about cursed masks; Anime Nights screened it tonight too. **Oct. 4:** *HOTEL INHUMANS* Season 2, the assassin-hotel show, for anyone who liked *John Wick* more than the plot of *John Wick*. **Oct. 13:** *DARK MACHINE THE ANIMATION*, an esports-as-national-economy story that reads like a Kai Cenat fever dream. *PSYREN* is \"coming soon\" with no date.\n\n![HOTEL INHUMANS Season 2](https://www.awn.com/sites/default/files/styles/inline_medium/public/image/attached/1081399-hotel-inhumansteaser-visual03-1280.jpg?itok=flqLMenL \"Ao Tajima / Shogakukan via AWN|https://www.awn.com/news/crunchyroll-announces-massive-fall-2026-anime-lineup\")\n\n## The take\nThree shows carry this season for our audience: *Overgeared* for the gamers, *Black Clover* for the shonen faithful, *Aoashi* for the sports crowd that never admits it watches anime. Everything else is a Tuesday. Dub dates are still TBA for most of it, so if you're a dub household, your season starts a few weeks late.\n\n## Sources\n- [Fall Anime 2026 on Crunchyroll: full schedule](https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/seasonal-lineup/2026/9/15/fall-anime-2026-crunchyroll) — Crunchyroll News, Sept. 15, 2026\n- [Crunchyroll Announces Massive Fall 2026 Anime Lineup](https://www.awn.com/news/crunchyroll-announces-massive-fall-2026-anime-lineup) — Animation World Network, Sept. 15, 2026\n- [Crunchyroll Anime Nights September sneak peek](https://www.crunchyroll.com/news/announcements/2026/9/1/crunchyroll-anime-nights-september-sneak-peek-tickets-on-sale) — Crunchyroll, Sept. 2026",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "publishedAt": "2026-09-21",
    "goLiveAt": "2026-09-21"
