    "slug": "cyberpunk-night-city-quiet-week-witcher-3-remastered-september-29-edgerunners-2-28-days-cd-projekt-calendar-2026",
    "pillar": "gaming",
    "title": "Night City's Quiet Week: CD Projekt's Calendar",
    "headline": "Night City's Quiet Week:\nCDPR's Next 28 Days",
    "subhead": "No new Cyberpunk patch this week, and that's the story. The Witcher 3 Remastered lands in seven days as a free update, Edgerunners 2 hits Netflix in 28, and the sequel sits on the engine CDPR chose this month.",
    "description": "Cyberpunk's standing beat: nothing new from Night City this week, so here's CD Projekt's calendar. Witcher 3 Remastered Sept. 29, Edgerunners 2 Oct. 20, Orion.",
    "keywords": [
      "Cyberpunk 2077",
      "Cyberpunk 2077 news",
      "CD Projekt Red",
      "The Witcher 3 Remastered",
      "Witcher 3 Remastered September 29",
      "Songs of the Past",
      "Cyberpunk Edgerunners 2",
      "Edgerunners 2 October 20",
      "Project Orion",
      "Cyberpunk Battle.net",
      "Geralt Diablo 4 skin",
      "Sneakz and Beatz",
      "PHRHX",
      "Black-owned media"
    ],
    "ogHeadline": "NIGHT CITY'S QUIET WEEK:\nCDPR'S NEXT 28 DAYS",
    "ogAccent": "F3E600",
    "heroImage": "https://www.videogameschronicle.com/files/2026/08/cd-projekt-blizzard.jpg",
    "heroCredit": "CD Projekt Red / Blizzard via VGC",
    "heroCreditUrl": "https://www.videogameschronicle.com/news/geralt-of-rivia-makes-his-debut-in-diablo-4-as-the-witcher-3-remastered-launches-on-battle-net/",
    "heroFocus": "center",
    "trendScore": 70,
    "body": "Some weeks Night City doesn't post. Cyberpunk's official news page hasn't moved since the December anniversary drop, and there's no patch note to read you. So this is the calendar instead, because the next month is the busiest CD Projekt has had since Phantom Liberty.\n\n## Seven days: The Witcher 3 Remastered\nSeptember 29. Free update for anyone who owns the game, on every platform, and for the first time on Battle.net. Visual upgrades, both expansions, quality-of-life fixes, community-made mods folded in with the modders credited. Buy the new Songs of the Past expansion on Battle.net and you get a Geralt skin in Diablo 4; the skin also comes to anyone who buys the expansion when it launches fully next year. ([VGC](https://www.videogameschronicle.com/news/geralt-of-rivia-makes-his-debut-in-diablo-4-as-the-witcher-3-remastered-launches-on-battle-net/))\n\nWhy it's a Cyberpunk story: Cyberpunk 2077 and Phantom Liberty follow to Battle.net \"later this year,\" per CDPR's [BlizzCon announcement](https://press.cdprojektred.com/en/news/1847/cyberpunk-2077-comes-to-battle-net). The Witcher is the test run for the storefront Night City moves into next.\n\n## Twenty-eight days: Edgerunners 2\nOctober 20 on Netflix, Studio Trigger, the new crew. The supporting cast, the Cure opening and the Overwatch crossover have all been covered here; the count is the only new number. If you haven't rewatched season one, you have four weekends.\n\n## The engine\nCo-CEO Michał Nowakowski said last week that the move to Unreal Engine 5 \"was not the Cyberpunk launch,\" it was seeing Epic's Matrix demo. Orion, the Cyberpunk sequel being built in Boston, lives on that engine. So the quiet is real work: The Witcher 4 is the first UE5 game, Orion is the second, and there's nothing to patch on the old one because the old one is done at 40 million sold.\n\n## The honest line\nStanding beats don't get to fake news. This week the Cyberpunk story is a release date for a different game and a countdown for a cartoon. Both are worth your calendar. Neither is a headline. Say that on air and move.\n\n## Sources\n- [Geralt of Rivia makes his debut in Diablo 4 as The Witcher 3 Remastered launches on Battle.net](https://www.videogameschronicle.com/news/geralt-of-rivia-makes-his-debut-in-diablo-4-as-the-witcher-3-remastered-launches-on-battle-net/) — VGC, Aug. 26, 2026\n- [Cyberpunk 2077 comes to Battle.net](https://press.cdprojektred.com/en/news/1847/cyberpunk-2077-comes-to-battle-net) — CD Projekt Red Press Center\n- [CD Projekt Red's move from REDengine to UE5 wasn't because of Cyberpunk's launch](https://www.videogameschronicle.com/news/cd-projekt-reds-move-from-redengine-to-ue5-for-the-witcher-4-wasnt-because-of-cyberpunks-launch-co-ceo-says/) — VGC, Sept. 18, 2026\n- [Cyberpunk news page](https://www.cyberpunk.net/en/news/) — cyberpunk.net\n",
